# Gapless fast path, part 2 of 6: the loader gate cave.
name: gapless-2-gate-cave
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03051664
gate: build refuses unless the 32 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: The gate, entered from the hook at 0x0306cb2c (0021) with
  r0 = decoder module id. It re-executes the two displaced instructions
  (push {r4,r5,r6,lr}; mov r5, r0), loads the retained-module word from
  the state pair at 0x030515b0 (0020) via a PC-relative SUB.W, masks off
  the fast-path flag (lsls/lsrs #25), and compares against the requested
  module. On the stock path it records the requested module as retained
  and branches to 0x0306cb30, running the stock reset-and-start body
  unchanged. On a match (reachable only with the ARM patch 0026, which
  turns the compare's following branch into `beq` to the skip block) it
  records module|0x80 as retained -- the flag the delay cut (0023)
  tests -- and returns to the calling codec case, skipping the image
  re-copy, the core-1 reset, the parameter-page re-copy and the ready
  poll entirely; the rest of the stock load-start (the 0x65 info
  exchange in 0x03088824 and everything after) still runs. As shipped
  (no 0026) the compare result is ignored by an unconditional branch
  to the stock path, so behaviour is byte-equivalent to stock plus two
  writes to patch-owned state. The cave occupies 16 `bx lr` stub slots
  at 0x03051664..0x03051683 in the module-0 stub farm: the exhaustive
  reference scan (BL/B.W targets, literal words, MOVW/MOVT pairs, all
  82 modules) shows zero references to the whole range, the function
  before it ends in `pop {r4,r5,r6,pc}` at 0x03051662 so nothing falls
  through into it, and the referenced stub at 0x0305168a and the slot
  at 0x03051688 are deliberately left byte-identical.
